    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0112" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg12"/>

                <head>No. 10.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Osborn.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7,
                        1880</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 121.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 266 and incisures, relative to the “South American Continental Exhibition,”
                    which is to be held at Buenos Ayres, in September next, and to observe in reply
                    that, although it is not understood that the concurrence of this government in
                    the enterprise is invited, the United States feel much interest in the same, as
                    tending to increase the commercial and agricultural prosperity of the Argentine
                    Republic; and publicity has been given to the notification of the enterprise
                    through the public press and the Department of Agriculture.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
